<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chongzhen Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1611">1611</a>–<a href="/years/1644">1644</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Zhu Youjian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chongzhen Emperor (1611–1644) was the last emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a>, reigning from 1627. Inheriting an empire beset by famine, peasant rebellions and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> invasions, he executed or dismissed many ministers and generals, including the commander Yuan Chonghuan. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-zicheng">Li Zicheng</a>'s rebels took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> in April 1644, he hanged himself on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">Coal</a> Hill behind the Forbidden City.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chongzhen-emperor.jpg" alt="Chongzhen Emperor" width="320" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chongzhen-Emperor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
